            <ArticleTitle>GIW and InCoB are advancing bioinformatics in the Asia-Pacific.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>I1</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1186/1471-2105-16-S18-I1</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>GIW/InCoB2015 the joint 26th International Conference on Genome Informatics (GIW) and 14th International Conference on Bioinformatics (InCoB) held in Tokyo, September 9-11, 2015 was attended by over 200 delegates. Fifty-one out of 89 oral presentations were based on research articles accepted for publication in four BMC journal supplements and three other journals. Sixteen articles in this supplement and six articles in the BMC Systems Biology GIW/InCoB2015 Supplement are covered by this introduction. The topics range from genome informatics, protein structure informatics, image analysis to biological networks and biomarker discovery.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
